rough the shell. The system consists of an LLM with access to tools, a planner, and memory (see\\nFigure 16). The system is designed for deployment in an educational setting, a corporate setting, and to support\\nremote work environments such as Teams and Slack.\\n   Cabrero-Daniel et al. [2024] describe how LLM meeting assistants can improve agile software development\\nteam meetings, to generate favorable results for preparation and live assistance during Scrum meetings, although\\nsome testers remarked that LLM interventions felt unnatural and inflexible.\\n   A system to facilitate group conversations is MUCA [Mao et al., 2024], supporting What, When and Who\\nquestions, consisting of a sub-topic generator, dialog analyzer, and conversational strategies arbitrator. Wei et al.\\n\\n                                      Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research, Vol. 1, Article 1. Publication date: December 2025.\\n\"}]}\n", "output_truncated": false, "error": null, "tool_calls": [{"name": "run_command", "args": {"argv": ["python", "read_pdf.py", "--start-page", "23", "--end-page", "25"], "cwd": "."}, "result": {"argv": ["/mnt/d/Muiti-Agent Programing/agents/code-agent/24371220/.venv/bin/python", "read_pdf.py", "--start-page", "23", "--end-page", "25"], "cwd": "/home/ventsdenye/.local/state/code-agent/evaluations/run-nh47wiy_/results/paper/repo", "rc": 0, "stdout": "{\"pdf\": \"/home/ventsdenye/.local/state/code-agent/evaluations/run-nh47wiy_/results/paper/repo/paper.pdf\", \"pages\": [{\"page\": 23, \"text\": \"                                                                                                                  Agentic LLM     •   1:23\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n                  Fig. 13. Multi LLM agent framework with a planner, caller, summarizer [Shen et al., 2024]\\n\\n\\n\\nvision language model, they achieve target object grounding, achieving improved performance on an L-ZSON\\nbenchmark.\\n3.2.2 Action Tools. As we have seen in Section 2.3, LLM results ma