t have contents pages 1-2 etc in current context except not displayed. Could get_evidence by ev IDs if mapping sequential? Catalog total 43 and pages show IDs 24=16,25=17,26=18,27=10,28=16,29=19,30=20,... likely earlier reads mapping uncertain. Could call get_evidence \"ev-000001\" etc; each call pins one evidence, could use multiple get_evidence calls in one request? Yes multiple tools per code block. We can request e.g. get_evidence for 1-10? That would flood. But we need specific pages. Better use read_pdf targeted pages 1-2, 9-11, 14-16, 23-25 perhaps. However must not exceed 32k request body; each tool result comes before next model call, not same body? Tool call responses are added; system computes each API request body including conversation history? It says each true API request complete JSON body <=32000 incl messages/tools. Runtime likely trims context to visible evidence but perhaps keeps requested pages. Huge outputs if reading 4 pages at once may exceed next request. Current request includes 4 pages content ~16k plus system maybe already near? It seems current request body maybe 20k. Need be cautious.\n\nWe can use command read_pdf batches and command_result; then save note in same next request? Tool outputs are presented before next model response. We can in one code block call read_pdf(34-37), then save_note? Save_note content must be based on evidence visible in request (presented after tool result? no, within same code block tool results returned sequentially but model hasn't seen them when composing calls; cannot note yet). So strategy: one request read batch 3-4 pages; next request ask for pages and save notes based on just read pages. But content visible in next request. We can combine save_note plus next read_pdf in same response, since save_note content from previous request's evidence. Good.\n\nNeed produce five notes. We need actual content. Current visible pages 31-33 and 26. But notes should cover content from each theme. Need pages 1-... Let's map paper structure. Need answer exact:\n\nOverview: categories three categories - likely \"reasoning, acting, interacting\" (from conclusion says three capabilities? Need evidence). Search methods: authors first used keyword search? Then snowballing? Need page 3/4 exact. Need identify \"We first searched ... then ...\". Could infer: initial search via Google Scholar? followed by \"snowballing\" and \"expert recommendations\"? Let's read pages 1-5.\n\nReasoning: Self Consistency selection rule: \"majority vote\" likely. Tree of Thoughts two search controllers: BFS and DFS. Need evidence exact page 10? Could answer majority voting; breadth-first and depth-first search. Need quote.\n\nTool use: Toolformer five tools: calculator, question answering, machine translation, web search, calendar? Toolformer paper tools: calculator, question answering, machine translation, Wikipedia search, calendar. In survey likely \"calculator, question answering, machine translation, web search, and calendar\". ToolBench API count: 16,464 APIs? ToolBench (Qin et al. 2023) collects 16,464 real-world APIs. Likely.\n\nMulti-agent: CAMEL uses \"inception prompting\" (role-playing with inception prompt). Paper says \"CAMEL uses inception prompting\". Generative Agents evaluators: 100 human evaluators? Need exact. I recall Generative Agents evaluation had 100 human evaluators. Could be 100.\n\nOutlook: Table 4 five research topics likely \"safety, interpretability, ...\". Need exact table. Conclusion three abilities benefit from two foundational abilities: \"reasoning\" and \"planning\"? Paper's taxonomy three categories: reasoning, acting, interacting. Shared foundations perhaps \"planning and memory\"? Need read conclusion.\n\nWe must read all pages anyway. Let's continue. Current request isn't a tool call; namespace shows no latest action. We need output code. We'll read pages 34-37."}, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop"}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 9063, "completion_tokens": 1282, "total_tokens": 10345, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 3840}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1251}, "prompt_cache_hit_tokens": 3840, "prompt_cache_miss_tokens": 5223}, "system_fingerprint": "bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}, "elapsed_seconds": 10.103085205999946, "timeout_seconds": 210.0, "remaining_seconds": 1637.5681588390003}
